---
/**
 * The static Week 8 specimen: the same four structural categories in two
 * orders, with the adjacency note that changes between them.
 *
 * This is the homepage's fallback for the optional Load Tester, which has not
 * been built. It is deliberately not interactive and makes no claim to be ---
 * plan.md is explicit that the core homepage must never carry a broken,
 * disabled or "coming soon" control.
 */
---

<svg class="los" viewBox="0 0 420 200" role="img" aria-labelledby="los-t los-d" focusable="false">
  <title id="los-t">The same four layers in two assembly orders</title>
  <desc id="los-d">
    Two exploded stacks side by side. In the first, the moist layer sits
    directly against the outer layer. In the second, the binding layer has been
    moved between them.
  </desc>
  <g class="los-stack">
    <rect x="24" y="30" width="150" height="16" />
    <rect class="los-moist" x="24" y="56" width="150" height="16" />
    <rect x="24" y="82" width="150" height="16" />
    <rect x="24" y="108" width="150" height="16" />
    <rect x="24" y="134" width="150" height="16" />
  </g>
  <path class="los-arrow" d="M198 92 h24 m-7 -6 l7 6 l-7 6" aria-hidden="true" />
  <g class="los-stack">
    <rect x="246" y="30" width="150" height="16" />
    <rect x="246" y="56" width="150" height="16" />
    <rect class="los-moist" x="246" y="82" width="150" height="16" />
    <rect x="246" y="108" width="150" height="16" />
    <rect x="246" y="134" width="150" height="16" />
  </g>
</svg>

<style>
  .los { width: 100%; height: auto; display: block; }
  .los-stack rect {
    fill: var(--slop-paper);
    stroke: var(--slop-charcoal);
    stroke-width: 1.5;
  }
  /* Moisture, not load --- so brown rather than red. */
  .los-moist {
    fill: color-mix(in srgb, var(--slop-toast) 34%, var(--slop-paper));
    stroke: var(--slop-toast);
  }
  .los-arrow {
    fill: none;
    stroke: var(--slop-charcoal);
    stroke-width: 1.8;
    stroke-linecap: round;
    stroke-linejoin: round;
  }
</style>
